\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc0}{\*\bkmkend toc0}\b \uc2  China's Yuan Ends Slightly Higher; No Reaction To Fed \b0\par\par\uc2 247 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2001\par 05:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan ended slightly stronger against the U.S. dollar Wednesday on selling of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by banks on behalf of exporters. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 8.2766 yuan compared with CNY8.2767 Tuesday. It traded in a tight range between CNY8.2765 and CNY8.2767. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there was no reaction in China's highly-regulated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to news that the U.S. Federal Reserve Tuesday cut the federal-funds rate by 50 basis points to 2%. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to make sure the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate doesn't stray too far from its ordinary trading range. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is widely considered to have an unofficial trading band of between around CNY8.2770 and CNY8.2800. \par \par \uc2  However, the yuan has frequently moved below CNY8.2770 in recent months, prompting speculation that authorities are attempting to quietly widen the band ahead of China's entry into the World Trade Organization, expected early next year at the latest. \par \par \uc2  The yuan can only be converted for current account purposes, and most exporters are required to repatriate 85% of their export receipts to state-owned commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Hong Kong dollar ended flat at CNY1.0604, and the Japanese yen rose to CNY6.8472 per 100 yen from CNY6.8007. \par \par \uc2  -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011107dxb700074\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
