\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc1}{\*\bkmkend toc1}\b \uc2  China's Yuan Ends Slightly Up On Exporter Dollar Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2001\par 04:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan closed slightly firmer against the U.S. dollar Tuesday on dollar-selling by banks on behalf of exporters. \par \par \uc2  It was the second day in a row that the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at CNY8.2767, down from CNY8.2768 Monday, after trading in a wide range between CNY8.2669 and CNY8.2769. \par \par \uc2  However, "only a very small number (of deals) were seen at CNY8.2669, which we think might be an input error, and most of the deals were actually conducted around 8.2767," said a trader at Industrial & Commercial Bank of China in Beijing. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is widely considered to have an unofficial trading band of between around CNY8.2770 and CNY8.2800. \par \par \uc2  However, the yuan has frequently dropped below CNY8.2770 in recent months, prompting speculation that authorities are attempting to quietly widen the band ahead of China's entry into the World Trade Organization, expected early next year at the latest. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, wouldn't allow the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stray too far from the trading band, traders say. \par \par \uc2  The yuan can only be converted for trade purposes and most exporters are required to repatriate 85% of their export receipts to state-owned banks. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar ended flat at CNY1.0604 and the Japanese yen rose to CNY6.8007 per 100 yen from Monday's CNY6.7926. \par \par \uc2  -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011106dxb60006w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
