\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc6}{\*\bkmkend toc6}\b \uc2  China yuan ends firmer, outside usual tight band. \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2001\par 05:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 23 (Reuters) - China's yuan gained ground against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, riding an abundant hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply from domestic banks. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2768 to one dollar, compared with Wednesday's 8.2770. Turnover was not immediately available. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said strong dollar sales by banks, which acquired the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from domestic exporters, supported the yuan and pushed it to 8.2770, the firm end of its usual trading band. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan was almost flat and hit only three notches today," said a Chinese bank dealer in Shanghai. "Banks kept selling dollars, extending the yuan's firmness." \par \par \uc2  The exchange rate is mainly driven by China's trade performance as the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only convertible on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said China's trade surplus - $10.08 billion for the first seven months of 2001 - would continue to bolster the yuan in the short term. \par \par \uc2  The central People's Bank of China boxed the yuan between 8.2770 and 8.2800 from mid-1997 to April 2000, but has since eased its grip and allowed the yuan to close marginally outside that range on a fairly regular basis. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's impending entry to the World Trade Organisation appears to be pushing authorities to consider a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, but some analysts speculate Beijing is unlikely to devalue the yuan until the current government term ends in 2003. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the yuan firmed to end at 6.8679 against 100 Japanese yen versus 6.8998 on Wednesday. It also strengthened to finish at 1.0605 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0611. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010823dx8n006y4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
