\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc7}{\*\bkmkend toc7}\b \uc2  China yuan ends slightly weaker, ignores Fed cut. \b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2001\par 07:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 22 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed a touch softer against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, as the Federal Reserve's overnight U.S. interest rate cut caused nary a ripple on the tightly controlled Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2770, one notch weaker than Tuesday's close, but dealers said the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained solid as abundant dollar supply from banks continued to keep the yuan trading tightly around the firm end of its usual trading band. \par \par \uc2  Turnover swelled to a robust $400 million from a decent $290 million. \par \par \uc2  The Fed on Tuesday cut interest rates by a quarter percentage point, its seventh reduction this year, and signalled it was poised to do more to help the U.S. economy battle weakness at home and abroad. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect China to cut interest rates for domestic dollar savings soon, as it had followed Fed moves six times this year. \par \par \uc2  But the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tight grip on the yuan leaves little speculative room in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. The yuan exchange rate is mainly driven by China's trade performance as the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only convertible on the current account. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. rate cut did not affect trading here because the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is relatively insulated from overseas market moves," said a dealer at a foreign bank in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers noted that a narrower gap between onshore dollar and yuan savings rates would help curb illegal dollar hoarding and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  flight, and benefit the yuan's stability in the long run. \par \par \uc2  Following the six rate cuts, the interest rate for one-year dollar deposits in China stands at 2.5 percent, compared with 2.25 percent for the one-year yuan savings rate. \par \par \uc2  The central People's Bank of China contained the yuan between 8.2770 and 8.2800 from mid-1997 to April 2000, but has since eased its grip and allowed the yuan to close slightly outside that range on a fairly regular basis. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's impending entry to the World Trade Organisation appears to be pushing authorities to consider a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, but some analysts speculate Beijing is unlikely to devalue the yuan until the current government term ends in 2003. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan gave ground to end at 6.8998 against 100 Japanese yen versus 6.8465 on Tuesday. It also weakened to finish at 1.0611 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0606. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dx8m02bi2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
