\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc8}{\*\bkmkend toc8}\b \uc2  China yuan ends softer but still outside band. \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2001\par 07:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 21 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened by one notch against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday, but still ended outside the firm end of its usual thin band on healthy dollar supply from banks. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2769 to one dollar as turnover rose to a decent $290 million, compared with $270 million on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Banks that had acquired ample dollars from domestic exporters trimmed their hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions on the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The one notch fall did not change the yuan's solid trend because it still traded stronger than 8.2770 for the entire session," said a Chinese bank dealer in Beijing. \par \par \uc2  China's trade surplus - $10.08 billion for the first seven months of 2001 - has been supporting the yuan, which is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was expected to continue to trade around 8.2770, the firm end of its 30-notch trade band, in the near term. \par \par \uc2  The central People's Bank of China contained the yuan in the hair-thin range from mid-1997 to April 2000, but it has eased its grip and allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to close slightly outside the range on a fairly regular basis over the past 16 months. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's impending entry to the World Trade Organisation appears to be pushing authorities to consider a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, but some analysts speculate Beijing is unlikely to devalue the yuan until the current government term ends in 2003. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yuan firmed to end at 6.8465 against 100 Japanese yen versus 6.8672. It ended flat at 1.0606 against the Hong Kong dollar for the second straight session. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dx8l02gfd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
