\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc9}{\*\bkmkend toc9}\b \uc2  China's yuan ends unchanged, dollar supply solid. \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2001\par 07:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 20 (Reuters) - China's yuan ended flat at 8.2768 against the U.S. dollar on Monday as solid dollar supply from banks helped the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hold its strength. \par \par \uc2  Turnover climbed to a healthy $270 million from a moderate $200 million on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said banks that had acquired dollars from domestic exporters offloaded holdings on the Shanghai-based national market, underpinning the yuan which traded tightly around 8.2770, the firm end of its usual 30-notch trade band. \par \par \uc2  China's trade surplus is the key driver of the yuan's exchange rate because the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Official figures showed China had a trade surplus of $10.08 billion in the first seven months of 2001, although that was down nearly 30 percent from $14.34 billion in the same 2000 period. \par \par \uc2  "We do not expect strong dollar supply on the market would drop in the near term," said a Chinese bank dealer in Shenzhen. \par \par \uc2  The central People's Bank of China sandwiched the yuan in a narrow box of 8.2770 to 8.2800 from mid-1997 to April 2000, but it has eased its grip and allowed it to close slightly outside the range on a fairly regular basis over the past 16 months. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's impending entry to the World Trade Organisation appears to be pushing the government to consider a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, but some analysts speculate Beijing is unlikely to devalue the yuan until the current government term ends in 2003. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan strengthened to end at 6.8672 against 100 Japanese yen versus 6.8845. It ended unchanged at 1.0606 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dx8k0094b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
