\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc11}{\*\bkmkend toc11}\b \uc2  China's Yuan Ends Flat At 8.2769; Upward Bias Persists \b0\par\par\uc2 202 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2001\par 05:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan closed unchanged Monday at 8.2769 to the U.S. dollar as ample dollar supply from exporters put upward pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan vacillated between CNY8.2758 and CNY8.2771 throughout the session on volume of $220 million, slightly lower than Friday's $368 million. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has been rising since Wednesday on weak dollar demand from importers and strong dollar supply from exporters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  strictly monitors daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, making speculation virtually impossible. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they didn't detect any signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  is generally thought to maintain an unofficial yuan trading band between CNY8.2770 and CNY8.2800 to the dollar though the range has been frequently breached in recent sessions - leading to speculation that China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying out a wider band ahead of the country's WTO entry. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen slipped to CNY6.6485 per 100 yen from CNY6.6928. The Hong Kong dollar slid to 1.0605 from CNY1.0607. \par \par \uc2  -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010730dx7u00074\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2