\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc13}{\*\bkmkend toc13}\b \uc2  China's yuan closes strong, outside normal band. \b0\par\par\uc2 619 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2001\par 07:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, July 12 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed against the U.S. dollar to end outside its usual hair-thin trading band on Thursday as domestic banks sold dollars on behalf of exporters, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2768 to the dollar, up from Wednesday's 8.2775 and outside its longstanding band of 8.2770 to 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  It traded outside the band for most of the session, although it touched an intraday low of 8.2770 several times. \par \par \uc2  Sudden demand for the yuan about 10 minutes before the market closed pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an intraday high of 8.2760, but there was only one deal done at the level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar selling by domestic banks for exporters helped the yuan keep strong today," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Despite the yuan firmness, there was no sign the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  (PBOC) had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the strength of the domestic curreny on Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar selling from local banks was heavy today but buying was also active," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan's movements today did not indicate it was likely to rise further and there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Chinese companies have to sell most of their hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenues to domestic banks and buy it from banks using import documents. Banks balance their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Chinese banks have accumulated heavy dollar positions as China has posted a trade surplus since the start of last year, although the surplus began to decrease this year as the global economy slowed, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The government reported a trade surplus of $7.32 billion in the first five months of 2001, down from $10.46 billion in the same period of last year. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in the session to prevent the yuan from rising beyond 8.2768, dealers said. It was the first time the bank acted to curb yuan strength since late last year, they said. \par \par \uc2  The PBOC holds tight control over movements of the yuan, which is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  From mid-1997 to April 2000, it sandwiched the yuan between 8.2770 and 8.2800 to fend off speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But over the past 14 months, it has relaxed its grip to some extent and allowed the yuan to end outside that range 71 times, mostly outside the firm end. \par \par \uc2  Officials say the yuan will be given more flexibility to cope with changes on China's balance of payments after its entry to the World Trade Organisation. But they have not said what the new range would be. \par \par \uc2  China is expected to join the WTO by early 2002 at the latest and a rise in imports after entry coupled with slowing global demand for exports is likely to erode its trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was likely to remain strong in the near term around the 8.2770 level due to strong dollar supply on the market. But they said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not likely to let it close stronger than 8.2760. \par \par \uc2  "Market players are aware of the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to prevent the yuan from rising beyond 8.2760," said the U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "They are not likely to push the yuan above that level." \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the yuan weakened to end at 6.6535 against 100 Japanese yen, compared with Wednesday's 6.5870. It closed a touch weaker against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0607 from 1.0605. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx7c00b0u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
