\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc14}{\*\bkmkend toc14}\b \uc2  China Yuan Ends Weaker On Importer Dollar Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 244 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2001\par 06:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan finished weaker Wednesday on strong dollar buying by importers covering their regular foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirements, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at CNY8.2775 to the U.S. dollar compared with CNY8.2770 Tuesday. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved between CNY8.2768 and CNY8.2782 in the session. \par \par \uc2  "Trading was a bit volatile today, but there's nothing significant about the moves," a trader at Shanghai Pudong Development Bank said, adding that regular dollar demand just outpaced supply in Wednesday's trading. \par \par \uc2  A Beijing-based trader at Industrial and Commercial Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Wednesday's trading. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan can only be converted for current account transactions. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading is tightly monitored by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , virtually eliminating opportunities for speculative buying and selling. \par \par \uc2  China is generally thought to maintain an unofficial yuan trading band between CNY8.2770 and CNY8.2800 to the dollar. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has frequently breached that range in recent sessions - leading to speculation that China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is experimenting with a wider band ahead of the country's accession to the World Trade Organization, expected early next year. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar closed unchanged at CNY1.0605. The Japanese yen dropped to CNY6.5870 per 100 yen from CNY6.5900. \par \par \uc2  -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx7b00076\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
