\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc17}{\*\bkmkend toc17}\b \uc2  China's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  seen acting to cap yuan. \b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2001\par 07:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, July 10 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed a touch weaker against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday after the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yuan's strength, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2770 to the dollar, down from Monday's 8.2767, touching an intraday high of 8.2768 and a low of 8.2786. \par \par \uc2  It moved outside the strong end of its normal tight range of 8.2770 and 8.2800 for the most of the session until the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last 15 minutes to prevent the yuan from rising beyond 8.2768, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Turnover remained decent at $250 million on Tuesday, although that was down from $440 million on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan kept up a rising momentum today and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in the session to curb its upward trend," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is consistent with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of keeping the yuan stable," he said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of China (PBOC) declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  The PBOC holds tight control over movements of the yuan, which is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  From mid-1997 to April 2000, it sandwiched the yuan between 8.2770 and 8.2800 to fend off speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But over the past 14 months, it has relaxed its grip to some extent, allowing the yuan to end outside that range 70 times. \par \par \uc2  Officials say the government is considering a wider trading band to cope with changes to China's balance of payments after its entry to the World Trade Organisation, which is expected to occur early next year at the latest. \par \par \uc2  But they have given no timetable for the reform nor a new range for the yuan. \par \par \uc2  In a recent Reuters poll of 10 analysts, seven saw no change in 2001 to the current range, equivalent to a miniscule 0.02 percent up or down. One analyst saw a marginal widening to 0.04 percent while two expected a move of up to three percent. \par \par \uc2  The poll produced an average forecast of a yuan band of 2.78 percent up or down by the end of 2002. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was likely to remain strong in the near term around the 8.2770 level due to ample dollar supply on the market. They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not likely to let it close stronger than 8.2760. \par \par \uc2  Chinese banks, who balance their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, have accumulated heavy dollar positions as China has posted a trade surplus since the start of last year, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yuan fell slightly to end at 6.5900 to 100 Japanese yen, compared with Monday's 6.5856. It also edged down against the Hong Kong dollar to close at 1.0605 from 1.0603. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010710dx7a00anm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
