\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc20}{\*\bkmkend toc20}\b \uc2  China's yuan edges up, rate cut to lend support. \b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2001\par 02:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 28 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed a touch stronger against the dollar on Thursday and dealers said expectations that China would match a rate cut by the U.S. Federal Reserve would bolster the yuan in the near term. \par \par \uc2  It ended at 8.2770 to one dollar, compared with Wednesday's close of 8.2772, after moving in a narrow range of 8.2767 to 8.2772 as turnover rose to a heavy $270 million from $170 million. \par \par \uc2  The Fed cut U.S. interest rates on Wednesday by a modest quarter-percentage point, the sixth reduction this year. Dealers said they expected Beijing to follow suit with another interest rate cut for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits in China. \par \par \uc2  The central People's Bank of China has cut domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposit rates five times so far this year, each time in response to a similar move by the Fed. \par \par \uc2  China's interest rate for one-year \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits is now 2.6875 percent, down from five percent at the start of this year. \par \par \uc2  Another cut in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate, even a slight one, would push the rate nearer the 2.25 percent level for one-year local yuan savings. \par \par \uc2  "Companies have become more willing to sell dollars for the yuan after a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposit rate cuts both at home and abroad this year," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Lower interest on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits also led to corresponding falls in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans, pushing domestic banks to trim dollar positions for those in yuan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  POTENTIAL LIMITED \par \par \uc2  Despite Thursday's gains, dealers said the potential for major rises in the yuan to would be limited because exchange rates for the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were already strong. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has stayed around 8.2770, the strong end of its normal hair-thin trading band of 8.2770 and 8.2800, over the past two weeks due to ample dollar supply on the market. \par \par \uc2  Domestic banks have accumulated heavy dollar positions as China recorded regular healthy trade surpluses since the start of last year. The surplus is key to dollar supply on the market as the yuan is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan would move around 8.2770 in the near term, but there was little potential for it to close stronger than 8.2760. \par \par \uc2  From mid-1997 to April 2000, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan in the tight box of 8.2770 to 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  But over the past 14 months, the bank has relaxed its control to allow the yuan to end outside the thin range 67 times. \par \par \uc2  Officials say the government is considering a wider yuan trading band but have given no timetable or range. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan strengthened slightly to end at 6.6424 against 100 Japanese yen, compared with Wednesday's 6.6833. It weakened against the Hong Kong dollar to close at 1.0619 verses 1.0608. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx6s00h7x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
