\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc21}{\*\bkmkend toc21}\b \uc2  China's yuan edges down in late dollar buying. \b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2001\par 06:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 27 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed a touch weaker in thin trade on Wednesday, pushed back inside its long-standing trading band as domestic banks snapped up dollars late in the session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at an intraday low of 8.2772 to one dollar, compared with Tuesday's close of 8.2767. \par \par \uc2  For most of the session it stayed firmer than 8.2770, the strong end of its usual tight trading range of 8.2770 to 8.2800, and touched an intraday high of 8.2767. \par \par \uc2  Turnover was thin at $170 million, compared with $180 million on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan was depressed by late dollar buying from some domestic banks," said a local bank dealer. "The banks might have had some urgent dollar orders from importers." \par \par \uc2  Chinese trade companies are required to sell most \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  income to domestic banks designated to trade on the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. They buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the banks on the basis of import documents. \par \par \uc2  Chinese banks settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the market after trading with trade companies. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Wednesday's fall did not represent a trend and the yuan was likely to remain strong in the near term due to heavy dollar supply on the market. The yuan has stayed strong around 8.2770 over the past two weeks. \par \par \uc2  Domestic banks have accumulated heavy dollar positions as China recorded regular healthy trade surpluses since the start of last year. The surplus is key to dollar supply on the market as the yuan is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar supply would stay around 8.2770 in the near term, but there was little potential for it to close stronger than 8.2760. \par \par \uc2  From mid-1997 to April 2000, the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan in a tight box of 8.2770 to 8.2800. But over the past 14 months, the bank has relaxed its control to allow the yuan to end outside the thin range 67 times. \par \par \uc2  Officials say the government is considering a wider yuan trading band but have given no timetable or range. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan strengthed to end at 6.6833 against 100 Japanese yen, compared with Tuesday's 6.7030. It weakened against the Hong Kong dollar to close at 1.0608 verses 1.0603. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6r00qro\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
