\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc22}{\*\bkmkend toc22}\b \uc2  China's yuan maintains strength, outside band again. \b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2001\par 07:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 26 (Reuters) - Heavy dollar supply helped China's yuan close unchanged against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday, outside the strong end of its normal tight trading band for a fourth straight session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said domestic banks had accumulated heavy dollar positions as China recorded regular healthy trade surpluses since the start of last year, keeping the yuan strong. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2767 to one dollar, outside its usual thin trading range of 8.2770 to 8.2800. It moved in a narrow range of 8.2766 to 8.2771 as turnover fell to a thin $180 million from $380 million. \par \par \uc2  "Strong dollar supply kept the yuan above the 8.2770 level for most of the session," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has maintained its strength to move around 8.2770 over the past two weeks. Dealers said there had been no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the period. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have quietly acknowledged a new range for the yuan with its strong end somewhere near 8.2760," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2720 on April 17, a record closing high since China's dual exchange rate system was unified in 1994. \par \par \uc2  From mid-1997 to April 2000, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan in a tight box of 8.2770 to 8.2800, partly to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But over the past 14 months, the bank has relaxed its control to allow the yuan to end outside the thin range 67 times, all but twice outside the strong end. \par \par \uc2  Officials say the government is considering a wider yuan trading band but give no timetable nor a new range. \par \par \uc2  The yuan's strength has been supported by the strong trade surplus, key to dollar supply on the market as the yuan is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Chinese trade companies are required to sell most \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  income to domestic banks designated to trade on the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. They buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the banks on the basis of import documents. \par \par \uc2  Chinese banks settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the market after trading with trade companies. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar supply would keep the yuan at high levels around 8.2770 in the near term but there was little potential for it to close stronger than 8.2760. \par \par \uc2  The yuan weakened to end at 6.7030 against 100 Japanese yen, compared with Monday's 6.6682. It strengthened against the Hong Kong dollar to close at 1.0603 verses 1.0609. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6q00wxm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
