\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc23}{\*\bkmkend toc23}\b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Asia: New Taiwan Dlr Faces Slow  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves Growth \b0\par\par\uc2  By J.R. Wu \par \uc2 957 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2001\par 07:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    A Dow Jones Newswires Column\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIPEI -(Dow Jones)- Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves aren't growing\par as fast as they used to, and that could influence the efforts of the\par country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend the New Taiwan dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  While that is not to say Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't have the ammunition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when it has to, dealers and observers remain watchful of the size of the foreign reserves coffers as an indication of whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be inclined to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and how aggressively it would do so. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell US$1 billion at the end of May to US$110.64 billion, the first monthly decline in five months. At those levels, the reserves still rank among the highest in the world. \par \par \uc2  But the outlook for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which has fallen as much as 4.4% this year so far - remains worrisome. \par \par \uc2  When the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave up its aggressive defense of the local dollar in May after spending roughly US$1 billion, dealers and analysts say it was allowing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stay competitive in the export markets amid the economic slowdown - rather than out of any worries for reserves. \par \par \uc2  Though pressure has eased on the local dollar since it fell to a 32-month low late last month, its direction remains decidedly down as anticipation mounts that the island's growth this quarter could contract for the first time in 26 years. \par \par \uc2  Reflecting this pessimism, the offshore market is pricing the New Taiwan dollar's one-month non-deliverable forwards at a spot price equivalent to around NT$34.40 to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, compared with the spot rate of NT$34.235 around midday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a foreign bank in Taipei thinks the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't let reserves fall too significantly before coming up with other measures to substitute for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts. \par \par \uc2  With reserves levels, "it's more about maintaining confidence," he says, adding that investor confidence would sink if reserves declined too sharply. \par \par \uc2  Before the decline in May, reserves grew 4.6% between December and April. Prior to that period, reserves fell for six straight months, or 6.2% from a record high of US$113.83 billion last July. \par \par \uc2  Reserves haven't slid under the US$100 billion level on a yearly basis since 1998 in part because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also replenishes its reserves by buying U.S. dollars whenever the greenback falls against the local dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Bulk Of Reserves In US Dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bulk of Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves is held in U.S.\par dollars, with the euro and yen making up much of the remainder of its\par portfolio.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers estimate roughly US$500 million are added to reserves each\par month just from interest alone. Foreign investor inflows and the monthly\par trade surplus figures also give some indication of possible gains in\par reserves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In May, the island's trade surplus expanded to US$1.22 billion from\par April's US$356.2 million as imports fell 29.6% on year, while exports\par declined a slightly smaller 22.6%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But even factoring all that, "growth has been very, very slow...only\par in the few hundred million a month," says another dealer at a foreign\par bank in Taipei.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dealer suspects so-called out-of-the-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par activities might have increased. These activities include those\par transactions conducted directly between counterparties that bypass\par Taiwan's two official central \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  brokerages.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Out-of-the-market transactions usually are related to interbank\par activity, but sometimes can be dealt between a corporate and a bank to\par avoid the brokerage fee, or directly with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with the aim\par to take pressure off the local dollar, especially in times of stress.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government's military purchases, Chinese Petroleum Corp.'s (Q.CPC)\par regular oil product imports, downpayment for commercial aircraft\par purchases or infrastructure-related equipment purchases are some\par examples of sizeable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Out-of-the-market transactions wouldn't show up on the spot pricing\par for the local dollar, but would be accounted for in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves if it was big enough.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, out-of-the-market transactions aren't large, which means the\par posted spot pricing and volume of daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  activity isn't\par being distorted too much, says an official in the domestic funding\par division at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of China.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But she adds this kind of activity increases as trading volume\par increases.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Even though the accumulation in reserves is likely to be slow, the New\par Taiwan dollar isn't likely to slide beyond NT$34.50 to the U.S. dollar\par for the moment, analysts reckon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That's where the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  settled on May 28 when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unexpectedly decided to halt aggressive all-day \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par efforts during the last half hour of trading, sending total \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading volume that day to US$2.02 billion, near record highs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The move came one session after the government said Taiwan's first\par quarter gross domestic product grew a worse-than-expected 1.06%, the\par smallest quarterly growth since 1975.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, market participants stress forecasting the New Taiwan dollar's\par levels remains an inexact science, given the tightlipped stance of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . They also make predictions usually on the condition of\par anonymity for fear of "being treated to coffee" by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par officials - a local euphemism for being reprimanded by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    -By J.R. Wu, Dow Jones Newswires; 8862-2502-2557; jr.wu@dowjones.com\par -0- 13/06/01 05-00G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4258 5095 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx6d02oju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
