\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc26}{\*\bkmkend toc26}\b \uc2  China's yuan ends up as exporters settle dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 514 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2001\par 07:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 4 (Reuters) - China yuan firmed against the U.S. dollar in active trade on Monday as domestic banks sold dollars on behalf of Chinese exporters, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Domestic banks had heavy dollar positions in hand, offsetting the end of a ban on Friday which prevented \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits made after February 19 from being used to buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  B shares, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2768 to the dollar, compared with Friday's close of 8.2778 and out of the strong end of its normal thin trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2780. It moved in a narrow range, touching an intraday high of 8.2760 and a low of 8.2775. \par \par \uc2  Turnover remained heavy at $350 million on Monday from a hefty $390 million on Friday, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com.cn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com.cn}}}\uc2 , the Web site of the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "Domestic banks had ample dollars that they bought from exporters and their selling pushed up the yuan," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. Trade firms are required to sell most of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  income to domestic banks designated to trade on the market. \par \par \uc2  Importers can buy dollars from the banks using import documents. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Chinese banks had accumulated heavy dollar positions since the start of last year as China has posted healthy trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  They said the freeing of all \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits for B share trading had little impact on the market as the actual \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflow from Chinese banks was expected to be small. \par \par \uc2  Analysts estimate new deposits entering the share market could be $2-3 billion over the next month. Personal \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  savings at Chinese banks total more than $74 billion. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was strong last week, trading tightly around the 8.2770 mark, the firm end of its normal thin 30-notch trade band due to flush dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move mainly around 8.2770 in the near term and possibly close slightly outside the strong end of its normal thin trading band. \par \par \uc2  For about three years since mid-1997, the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sandwiched the yuan within the band through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fend off speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Over the past year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has eased its grip on the yuan and allowed it to close outside the band 60 times, although only twice outside the weak end. There was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Officials say the government is considering a wider range for the yuan's exchange rate to cushion trade shocks expected from the China's accession to the World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  But they have given no timetable or range. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan strengthened to close at 6.9450 to 100 yen versus 6.9883 on Friday. It inched up two notch against the Hong Kong dollar to end at 1.0605 from 1.0607. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6402l4l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
