\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc27}{\*\bkmkend toc27}\b \uc2  China yuan a shade weaker, turnover climbs. \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2001\par 07:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 20 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday as demand for the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from local importers picked up. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2770 to one dollar, down from Tuesday's 8.2767, as turnover declined to a moderate $180 million from a decent $240 million, indicating easing dollar sales by banks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar bids picked up midway through the session, pulling the yuan down to around 8.2779 until minutes before the closing bell. \par \par \uc2  "More banks were buying dollars today and such bids became quite active after the middle of the trading," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. Banks typically settle \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the Shanghai-based national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients like importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Despite the Wednesday's fall, dealers said the yuan was expected to trade around the firm end of its razor-thin band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 in the short term, underpinned by China's trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  For about three years since mid-1997, the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had enforced the 30-notch trade band through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But over the past year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has eased its grip on the yuan and allowed it to close outside the band nearly 60 times, although only twice outside the weak end. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Officials say the government is considering a wider range for the yuan's exchange rates to cushion trade shocks expected from the China's accession to the World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  But they have given no timetable or a range. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan lost ground to close at 6.8798 to 100 yen versus 6.8282. It also weakened against the Hong Kong dollar to end at 1.0614, compared with 1.0609 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx5u02tjs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
