\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc33}{\*\bkmkend toc33}\b \uc2  China's yuan edges up, monetary policy no impact. \b0\par\par\uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2001\par 07:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, April 23 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed three-notches stronger against the U.S. dollar on Monday as exporters offered more hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following two days of slow supply. \par \par \uc2  The yuan finished at 8.2772 to one dollar, compared with Friday's 8.2775, as turnover expanded to a healthy $270 million from a light $150 million. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the waxing turnover and rising yuan indicated a pick-up in dollar supply, helping lift the yuan from a relatively weak 8.2775, at which it had closed flat in the previous two sessions. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Domestic banks typically settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mainly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's pledge to keep interest rates stable and the yuan exchange rate "basically stable" had no impact on the yuan trade on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "We should maintain steady growth in money supply, while keeping deposit and lending rates stable and the yuan exchange rate basically stable," state media quoted a statement from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Committee as saying after its second quarter regular meeting. \par \par \uc2  The term "basically stable" surprised few dealers, who viewed it as consistent with statements by the policy committee made since late last year. \par \par \uc2  "This is not a new policy term, we have come across the word since last October, although few people seem to understand how the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  defines its criteria for 'basically'," said a dealer at an European bank in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  Although China's latest monetary directives did not make any aggressive steps forward, dealers said Beijing still appeared to be preparing for a more flexible yuan. \par \par \uc2  Early this month, state media quoted a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator as saying China may allow the yuan to move in a wider daily range of up to 0.3 percent up or down to relax its rigid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime and help local markets adapt gradually to exchange rate volatility. They gave no timetable or further details. \par \par \uc2  Regulations on the Shanghai-based \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market set up in 1994 already allow the yuan to move up to 0.3 percent higher or lower than the weighted average price logged in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  But for most of the past three years, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent the yuan from closing outside a range of 8.2770 to 8.2800 to the dollar, to deter speculation over a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Although a 0.3 percent range would still be narrow under international standards, it would be significantly wider than the current band, equivalent to 0.018 percent up or down from the mid point. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they would trade more actively on the Shanghai \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the government allowed the yuan trade in the wider range. \par \par \uc2  "It would be good if they finally allow the yuan to trade between its nominal daily limits and still regard the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as stable in that range," said the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said a wider range could be just months away, noting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had become less active since April 2000 and allowed the yuan to close outside the band 51 times, although only twice outside its weak end. \par \par \uc2  China has vowed to make its rigid exchange rate regime more flexible to cushion trade shocks after it joins the World Trade Organisation, which may happen late this year. \par \par \uc2  Officials say that includes a wider band for the yuan, but they have given no timetable or range. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan edged weaker to close at 6.7710 against 100 yen from 6.7708. It strengthened against the Hong Kong dollar to end at 1.0607 versus 1.0613. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4n01lvc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
