\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc35}{\*\bkmkend toc35}\b \uc2  China's yuan ends weaker after hitting high. \b0\par\par\uc2 522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2001\par 07:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, April 18 (Reuters) - China's yuan softened against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday and closed just one notch outside the firm end of its usual trading band after setting a record closing high in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2769, down from Tuesday's 8.2720 which was the highest close since 1994 when China set up the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Tuesday's sudden surge was far from typical and was the result of a local bank putting in a last-minute order to sell dollars, apparently out of an urgent need of yuan. \par \par \uc2  "Trade went back to normal today," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. "Tuesday's extraordinary close did not reflect market reality and had no impact on trading today," he said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan moved in a narrow range of 8.2767 to 8.2773 on Wednesday. Turnover was a slim $100 million, down from an already sluggish $170 million on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  There was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support or depress the yuan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan in a wafer-thin, 30-notch range of 8.2770 to 8.2800 since mid-1997 partly to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But it has been less active since April 2000 and allowed the yuan to close outside the band 51 times, although only twice outside the weak end. \par \par \uc2  China has vowed to make its rigid exchange rate regime more flexible to cushion trade shocks after it joins the World Trade Organisation, which is expected later this year. \par \par \uc2  Officials say that includes a wider band for the yuan, although they have given no timetable or range. \par \par \uc2  In the past month, the yuan has been generally strong due to ample dollar supply in the market and China's healthy foreign trade surplus, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. Domestic banks usually settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mainly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves totalled $175.85 billion at the end of March, up 12.1 percent year-on-year and compared with $165.6 billion at the end of 2000. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys surplus dollars from the market to prevent the yuan from rising too sharply, resulting in rises in China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They saw limited potential for the yuan to rise further, partly due to expectations that exports growth would slow this year because of a global economic slowdown. \par \par \uc2  There had been growing reluctance among domestic banks to sell dollars in anticipation of less \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  income, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was likely to move narrowly around 8.2770 level in the near term, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan weakened to close at 6.7374 against 100 yen on Wednesday from 6.5389 on Tuesday. It ended unchanged against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0613. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4i01t5n\par }\page {\par\fs2