\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc43}{\*\bkmkend toc43}\b \uc2  China yuan firms as exporters sell dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2001\par 07:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, April 6 (Reuters) - China's yuan extended its rising streak on Friday, closing outside the strong end of its thin trade band for the third straight session as dollar sales by domestic exporters remained heavy. \par \par \uc2  The yuan inched up one notch to end at 8.2766 to one dollar as turnover waned to a still healthy $250 million from an active $280 million. \par \par \uc2  For most of the past three years, the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent the yuan from closing outside 8.2770 to 8.2800 to deter speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Friday, and Beijing appeared to be more tolerant when the yuan was firming. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar supply has picked up again after a few days of weakness last week," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account, which consists mainly of trade flows. \par \par \uc2  Banks typically settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the Shanghai-based national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mainly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Local exporters were expected to unload more dollars next week. But dealers said the yuan was unlikely to test its life high of 8.2761 logged on February 8 because too much strength might hinder China's exports, particularly when regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are weak. \par \par \uc2  The yuan, however, might continue to trade outside its long-standing band as Beijing appeared to be testing waters for a wider trade band to cushion against external trade shocks expected from its impending membership to the World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  Since April 2000, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has eased its grip, allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to close outside the usual range 47 times, though only twice outside the weak end of 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the yuan strengthened against the yen to close at 6.6194 versus 6.6331. It also edged up against the Hong Kong dollar to end at 1.0610 from 1.0614. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4602l3g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
