\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc44}{\*\bkmkend toc44}\b \uc2  China yuan ends firmer, outside thin band. \b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2001\par 07:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, April 4 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, ending outside the strong end of its slim trade band after a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator reaffirmed Beijing would make its rigid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime more flexible. \par \par \uc2  State media on Tuesday quoted a State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SAFE) official as saying China may allow its yuan to move in a daily range of up to 0.3 percent up or down to help market players gradually adapt to exchange rate volatility. \par \par \uc2  The official, deputy director of the Balance of Payments Department Zou Lin, did not give a timetable. \par \par \uc2  Regulations on the Shanghai-based \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market set up in 1994 already allow the yuan to move up to 0.3 percent higher or lower than the weighted average price logged a session earlier. \par \par \uc2  But for most of the past three years, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent the yuan from closing outside 8.2770 to 8.2800 to the dollar, to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan closed at 8.2768 to one dollar, compared with 8.2772 a session ago, as turnover fell to a moderate $200 million from an active $300 million. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the official remarks did not affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade, and the yuan's strength was underpinned by rising dollar supply from domestic exporters. The yuan is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  "The official comment did not make the yuan swing today because markets again took it as something symbolic," said a dealer at an European bank in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  "The point is: When will the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sit on its hands and let the yuan actually close at its up or down daily limit?" \par \par \uc2  WIDER RANGE IN THEORY \par \par \uc2  Based on Tuesday's weighted average price of 8.2772 announced by the Shanghai-based exchange, the yuan could, theoretically, move in a range between 8.2524 and 8.3020 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  However, the yuan touched an intraday high of 8.2768 and 8.2774 as there was no major imbalance between market supply and demand for the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Beijing should make further reforms to overhaul its current \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange settlement system, which keeps banks from speculating on the country's tiny and sluggish \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set a floor and ceiling requirement on how much \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange a bank could hold against the yuan. \par \par \uc2  Banks are required to settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions beyond those limits on the Shanghai-based national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mainly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  According to the semi-official China News Agency's report on Tuesday, Zou also said SAFE planned to relax restrictions on how much \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  a bank can hold against yuan assets, but gave no details. \par \par \uc2  Chinese officials have said the country would allow a wider trading band for the yuan to cushion against external trade shocks expected after it joins the World Trade Organisation. But they have not given a range nor timetable. \par \par \uc2  But Beijing, which expects WTO membership this year, appeared to have started testing the water already. \par \par \uc2  Since April 2000, the bank has eased its grip, allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to close outside the usual 30-notch range 45 times, although only twice outside the weak end of 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan closed firmer against the yen at 6.5874 versus 6.6930. It also edged up by three notches to end at 1.0611 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4402ozp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
