\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc45}{\*\bkmkend toc45}\b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Steadier, helped by yen, c.bank fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2001\par 03:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 4 (Reuters) - Soggy Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  got a brief break in early trade on Wednesday, thanks to a steadier yen and wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in some centres. \par \par \uc2  But brewing U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions, poor February semiconductor sales and a murky global economic picture should keep the dollar well-supported against the regionals, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was watching with growing interest as Beijing and Washington faced off over the spy plane affair after the U.S. EP-3 surveillance aircraft made an emergency landing on the island of Hainan. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Semiconductor Industry Association said on Tuesday that worldwide sales of semiconductors in February decreased 6.9 percent from January levels as the chip industry remained mired in a slump. \par \par \uc2  "Central banks in South Korea, Thailand and Singapore have sent a message to the market that they are not happy with the speed at which their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are falling. That should dent dollar demand a bit," said a dealer at an Asian bank. \par \par \uc2  "But the market is still pretty much in favour of the dollar because there are no fundamental changes to reverse that trend," he said. \par \par \uc2  The market is likely to watch closely comments by a slew of U.S. Federal Reserve speakers on Wednesday and Friday's March employment report, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters expect U.S. payrolls to have expanded by 58,000 new positions in March. They predicted the report would show the unemployment rate edged up to 4.3 percent, while average hourly earnings rose 0.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar mustered some strength on the firmer yen as the market began consolidating the dollar's recent big gains. \par \par \uc2  The euro's rise also triggered some selling of dollar/Sing. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank said dollar/Sing may trade down to 1.8050, close to Monday's low of 1.8055. But good dollar bids were expected around there. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's news that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was revising its 2001 growth forecast from 5-7 percent added to talk it may have changed its monetary policy stance to neutral. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said if the MAS were to formally announce a change, its impact would be limited as the market has already priced in a change to neutral from tightening given the absence of strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the much lower dollar/Sing. \par \par \uc2  "Even if they come out now and say that they've moving to a neutral policy stance I don't think it will have much of an impact because it's there already in the price," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht firmed in line with the yen and other regionals, with the market mindful of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's watchful eye. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said dollar/baht bounced higher after Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said in a televised address the economy was still saddled with problems and recovery would take time and effort. \par \par \uc2  But, with the market heavily long of dollars, players took profit at 45.40. Dealers said the Bank of Thailand's Tuesday warnings about acting to curb baht volatility were also making the market wary of actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was still stuck in overbought territory with a reading of 87.724 on the 14-day relative strength index. \par \par \uc2  However, players were still looking to buy dollars on dips, as the Constitutional Court began hearing corruption charges against Thaksin. \par \par \uc2  Offshore baht funding rates remained firm, providing some support to the dollar, and were quoted at 50/55 satang per dollar against 40/50 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won kept a softer tone at below 1,350 but did avoid revisiting 30-month lows of 1,355.0 hit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  It benefited in part from a wave of profit-taking on U.S. dollar longs, triggered by a senior finance ministry official's comments on Tuesday the government was in talks with U.S. and Japanese authorities on too rapid a fall of the yen. The remark came on the back of an estimated US$200 million sales by the Bank of Korea through state banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers raised concerns authorities were determined this time to smooth volatility in the won, which kept bears from further selling it. \par \par \uc2  But they said falling Korean shares after the Nasdaq's drop overnight would generate some equity-linked outflows, capping the won's upside at 1,330. \par \par \uc2  Vice economic ministers and the vice president of the Bank of Korea were due to discuss steps to stabilise the markets on Wednesday. Domestic media said the measures would call for lowering interest rates, stabilising the won, and attracting more investors into equities. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is likely to be caught between hopes for IMF funding approval and the poor political outlook against a backdrop of persistent corporate demand for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But wariness of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should help underpin the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "For now, the mood remains hesitant. And amid ongoing corporate demand, we would continue to expect that well-worn 10,300-10,500 range for dollar/rupiah, protected by official dollar offers," said IDEAglobal.com. Meanwhile, Japanese officials said Japan would soon agree with Indonesia over details of a sovereign debt restructuring plan, in line with a pact between the Paris Club and Jakarta to reschedule $5.8 billion in debt. \par \par \uc2  The Paris Club of creditor nations last year agreed to restructure $5.8 billion of Indonesia's sovereign debt, a little less than half of which is owed to Japan, they said. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso opened a touch softer, with dealers expecting it to move in a narrow range amid a dearth of fresh leads. \par \par \uc2  News of the Supreme Court rejecting ousted president Joseph Estrada's appeal that he was still president and immune from lawsuits provided little support for the peso as it was in line with market expectations. \par \par \uc2  The economic picture remained grim. Socio-economic planning Secretary Dante Canlas said on Tuesday the country might not be able to achieve the higher end of its 3.8-4.3 percent gross domestic product target in 2001 due to slower export growth. \par \par \uc2  The government is due to release March inflation data on Thursday. It predicted that the inflation rate would come in between 6.5-7.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar edged down to 32.94, threatening a key 33.00 support. \par \par \uc2  "I would expect the level would be easily breached within the next two to three trading sessions," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said mounting U.S.-China tensions drove foreign investors to sell equities and repatriate their funds. \par \par \uc2  This further reinforced the gloom over prospects of Taiwan's economy, bringing equity sales by foreigners to a net T$9.3 billion in the past five sessions, the strategist said. \par \par \uc2  "Any sharp fall in equities would hit the Taiwan dollar. The impact from that is now bigger than the yen," she said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0149 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     125.75\tab  125.54\tab    -0.17\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8095\tab  1.8120\tab    +0.14\par  Taiwan dlr    32.938\tab  32.900\tab    -0.12\par  Korean won   1345.10\tab 1343.00\tab    -0.16\par  Baht\tab      45.23\tab   45.20\tab    -0.07\par  Peso\tab      49.77\tab   49.70\tab    -0.14\par  Rupiah\tab 10453.00     10435.00\tab    -0.17\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     125.75\tab  114.45\tab    -8.99\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8095\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.03\par  Taiwan dlr    32.938\tab  32.900\tab    -0.12\par  Korean won   1345.10\tab 1277.00\tab    -5.06\par  Baht\tab      45.23\tab   43.70\tab    -3.38\par  Peso\tab      49.77\tab   50.75\tab    +1.97\par  Rupiah\tab 10453.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -9.40\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4402o4j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
