\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc46}{\*\bkmkend toc46}\b \uc2  China's yuan strengthens in heavy trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2001\par 07:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, April 3 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday in robust trade as strong dollar supply from domestic exporters flowed in. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2772 to the dollar versus Monday's 8.2775 as turnover swelled to a heavy $300 million from $240 million. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar sales were quite strong today, unlike the past few days," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Chinese banks typically settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the Shanghai-based national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mainly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan had held steady at 8.2775 in the last two sessions, catching its breath after sliding for three days early last week on stronger dollar demand from local importers. \par \par \uc2  The yuan's strength on Tuesday might not indicate a short-term firming trend as China's imports are likely to pick up in the second quarter and boost dollar demand, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  From 1997 through early 2000, the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep the yuan in a razor-thin band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 to the dollar to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But the bank has since eased its grip, allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to close outside the usual range 44 times since April 2000, although only twice outside the weak end of 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan weakened against the yen to close at 6.6930 on Tuesday versus 6.4818. It also edged down by three notches to end at 1.0614 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4302uwe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
