\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc49}{\*\bkmkend toc49}\b \uc2  China yuan ends flat in robust trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2001\par 08:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, April 2 (Reuters) - China's yuan held steady at 8.2775 against the U.S. dollar on Monday, catching its breath after sliding for three of the past four sessions due to stronger dollar demand from local importers early last week. \par \par \uc2  Turnover stood at a healthy $240 million, compared with $250 million on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "There were no big changes in market demand for dollars today, which was a bit strong," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has been leaning away from the 8.2770 mark, the firm end of its 30-notch trade band, since Tuesday as Chinese importers bought dollars for trade settlement. \par \par \uc2  Chinese banks typically settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the Shanghai market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mainly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to reverse a one-month uptrend since early March as China's imports are likely to pick up in the second quarter. \par \par \uc2  Trade performance is the key factor driving the value of the yuan, which is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  From 1997 through early 2000, the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to box the yuan in a tiny band to deter speculation of a yuan devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But the bank has since eased its grip, allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to close just outside its usual range 44 times since April 2000, although only twice outside the weak end at 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say Beijing is testing the waters for a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to cushion China from trade shocks after its entry to the World Trade Organisation, expected this year. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong last week re-affirmed a pledge that China would adopt a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rate after it joins the WTO, state media reported. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said they did not expect Beijing to give up defending the yuan at the key psychological 8.2800 mark in the near term. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan strengthened against the yen to end at 6.4818 versus 6.6780. It inched lower against the Hong Kong dollar to close at 1.0611, compared with 1.0609 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4202s92\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
