\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc51}{\*\bkmkend toc51}\b \uc2  UPDATE 2-China sees greater yuan flexibility after WTO. \b0\par\par\uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 09:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIJING, March 28 (Reuters) - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Dai Xianglong, expects a more flexible exchange rate after China joins the World Trade Organisation, state media said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "After WTO entry there will be bigger changes in the balance of payments along with changes in foreign trade and investment," the Financial News quoted Dai as saying in an interview with the U.S. based magazine BusinessWeek. \par \par \uc2  Talks on China's entry into the WTO are are likely to drag on at least until late this year. \par \par \uc2  "The exchange rate will have some flexibility," Dai said. \par \par \uc2  "But generally speaking we will continue to implement and improve the current exchange system," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dai said China's economy was now sound and "the yuan exchange rate is stable and has a solid foundation". \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to ensure the yuan trades within a wafer-thin band, partly to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trapped in a narrow band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 for more than three years after the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  But the bank seems to be relaxing its grip; it has allowed the yuan to close outside the hair-thin range more than 40 times since April 2000, though only twice outside the weak end. \par \par \uc2  It ended at 8.2775 on Wednesday against Tuesday's close of 8.2774 after moving in a relatively wide range of 8.2770 to 8.2790. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is convertible only on the current account, which mainly covers trade and services, and is now well supported by China's healthy balance of payments surplus. \par \par \uc2  Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is less likely to give up defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the psychological 8.2800 mark, at least this year, to deter speculation of a devaluation, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  SHARP MOVES UNLIKELY \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Beijing has been testing the waters for a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to cushion China from trade shocks after its entry to the WTO. \par \par \uc2  "The renminbi (yuan) exchange rate is expected to come under to looser controls after the WTO entry," said Song Guoqing, chief economist at the China Stock Exchange Council. \par \par \uc2  "But sharp fluctuations in the exchange rate are quite unlikely if inflation is checked, because any changes in the balance of payments can only happen gradually," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Dai's comments came as little surprise and had little impact on trading. \par \par \uc2  There was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support or depress the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Banks recently have had less \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  business to do due to China's falling trade surplus this year," said a dealer at a local bank. "A rough balance of dollar supply and demand made the yuan close almost unchanged today." \par \par \uc2  The trade surplus fell 17.85 percent to $2.37 billion in the first two months of this year against the year earlier period. \par \par \uc2  The inflow of foreign direct investment to China is also expected to rise after the country becomes a WTO member, offsetting pressure on the yuan from rising imports and slower exports. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3s030jz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
