\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc52}{\*\bkmkend toc52}\b \uc2  China yuan softer, local banks buy dlrs. \b0\par\par\uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 07:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, March 27 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed slightly softer in thin trade on Tuesday as local banks bought dollars on behalf of importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2774, compared with Monday's close of 8.2769 after moving in a narrow range of 8.2769 to 8.2775. \par \par \uc2  "Slight dollar buying by domestic banks on behalf of importers pushed the yuan's exchange rate down today," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "But the fall does not represent a trend as there is a rough balance of dollar demand and supply on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The yuan is likely to move narrowly around the current levels in the near term," he said. \par \par \uc2  Chinese banks typically settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the Shanghai-based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mainly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Importers are allowed to obtain \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on required trade-related documents while exporters must sell most of their hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings to banks. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has generally been strenghthening since late February as there was decent dollar supply on the market after Chinese banks accumulated heavy dollar positions last year when China scored a healthy foreign trade surplus, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But market turnover has dropped significantly since the start of March as China's foreign trade surplus was falling this year, making local banks reluctant to sell dollars in fears of reduced inflow of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  China's foreign trade surplus is key for dollar supply and demand on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market because the yuan is only convertible under the current account. \par \par \uc2  The trade surplus fell 17.85 percent to $2.37 billion in the first two months of this year against a year earlier period, official figures showed. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, turnover was only $130 million, although that was up from a slim $40 million from Monday, according to figures published on the market's website, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com.cn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com.cn}}}\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Average daily turnover has fallen to around $180 million in March from $402 million in February, exchange figures showed. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said turnover on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would likely remain thin in the near term due to expectations of China's slowing foreign trade. \par \par \uc2  Top Chinese officials have warned weak global economies would likely pressure China's exports, leading to slowing trade and dropping surplus in 2001 compared with 2000. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Over the past three years, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has enforced a wafer-thin trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 for the yuan through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , partly to quell speculation of a devaluation of the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the bank has reduced its activity in the past year, allowing the yuan to close outside the usual range 44 times since April 2000, but only twice outside the weak end. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Beijing is testing waters for a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to cushion China from trade shocks after its entry to the World Trade Organisation, which is expected this year. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was less likely to give up defending the yuan at the key psychological 8.2800 mark, at least this year, to deter speculation of a yuan devaluation, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yuan weakened to close at 6.7500 against 100 yen from 6.6928 on Monday. It fell slightly against the Hong Kong dollar to end at 1.0614 from 1.0612. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3r036uh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
