\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc55}{\*\bkmkend toc55}\b \uc2  China's yuan edges up in thin trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 06:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, March 16 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed up slightly against the U.S. dollar in thin trade on Friday as domestic banks conducted light dollar selling, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2770, compared with Thursday's close of 8.2774, after moving in a narrow range of 8.2768 to 8.2776. \par \par \uc2  "Slight dollar selling from local banks pushed up the yuan," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading volume on the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had fallen significantly since the start of March as domestic banks reported a reduced inflow of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an indication that China's trade surplus was narrowing. \par \par \uc2  Official figures issued this week showed China's trade surplus fell a year-on-year 17.85 percent to $2.37 billion in the first two months of 2001. \par \par \uc2  "We have seen a significant reduction in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflow over the past few weeks," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "As a result, our business on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is dropping," he said. \par \par \uc2  Trade is key to dollar supply on the market as the yuan is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Chinese banks typically settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the market after trading with corporate clients, mainly importers and exporters, who are required to sell most of their dollar earnings to banks. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, turnover was thin at $170 million, although that was up from $70 million on Thursday, according the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's website, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com.cn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com.cn}}}\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The average daily turnover this week was only $110 million, compared with $180 million last week and $402 million for February, according to exchange data. \par \par \uc2  Foreign Trade Minister Shi Guangsheng said on Tuesday trade growth was likely to slow in 2001 due to a weaker global economy. Dealers said they expected exports to grow by eight to 10 percent this year, compared with a surge of 27.8 percent last year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was likely to move in a narrow range between 8.2770 and 8.2780 in thin trade in the near term. \par \par \uc2  They said there was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the yuan in the wafer-thin trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for about three years, partly to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But the bank has reduced its activity in the past year, allowing the yuan to close outside the usual range more than 40 times since April 2000, although only twice outside the weak end. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say Beijing is moving towards a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to cushion China from trade shocks after its entry to the World Trade Organisation, probably this year. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the yuan strengthened to close at 6.7552 against 100 Japanese yen from 6.9352 on Thursday. It also firmed to end at 1.0610 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0615. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3g03zo2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
