\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc56}{\*\bkmkend toc56}\b \uc2  China Yuan Ends Up On Exporter Dlr Sales; Bonds Mostly Dn \b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 09:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan ended stronger against the dollar Thursday on exporter selling of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed lower at 8.2774 yuan compared with CNY8.2778 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  It traded in a narrow range between CNY8.2771 and CNY8.2778. \par \par \uc2  Volume shrank to US$70 million from the previous US$150 million. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar selling by exporters is still the primary driver of yuan trading," said a trader at Shanghai Pudong Development Bank. "We didn't see any particularly large deals conducted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  China's yuan can only be converted for trading purposes and most exporters must repatriate 85% of their overseas receipts to state-owned banks. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar rose to CNY1.0615 from CNY1.0610, and the Japanese yen dipped to CNY6.9352 per Y100 from CNY6.9764. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, government bonds closed mostly lower on profit-taking. \par \par \uc2  "Since bonds have been rising for four straight days, such profit-taking was expected sooner or later," said a trader at Shenyin & Wanguo Securities in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  The trader added that the market remains bullish overall because there haven't been many initial public offerings in the stock market recently, so there's less of an incentive for investors to sell bonds and buy stocks instead. \par \par \uc2  The 1999 10-year bond retreated CNY0.28 to CNY101.71 on trade of 629,095 lots. Its yield increased to 3.28% from 3.24%. \par \par \uc2  The 2000 10-year floating-rate bond shed CNY0.14 to CNY103.71 on trade of 327,066 lots. \par \par \uc2  The only issue bucking the trend was the 1997 10-year bond, which jumped CNY0.11 to CNY138.44 on trade of 165,397 lots. Its yield slid to 3.86% from 3.87%. \par \par \uc2  Total transaction volume was CNY1.94 billion, below CNY2.13 billion Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  China's bond market is off-limits to foreign investors. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268;\par djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com\par -0- 15/03/01 08-27G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3f015v9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
