\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc57}{\*\bkmkend toc57}\b \uc2  China's yuan inches up in listless trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 06:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, March 14 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed a touch firmer against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday as local banks conducted light dollar selling on behalf of experters, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was listless as China's slowing foreign trade growth led to reduced need for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  business, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2778, compared with Tuesday's close of 8.2780, after moving in a narrow range of 8.2777 to 8.2785. \par \par \uc2  "Slight dollar selling from domestic banks pushed up the yuan," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "But overall trading was listless as China's slowing foreign trade has reduced business needs. The trend is likely to continue in the near term," he said. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. Banks typically settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mostly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Official figures issued this week showed China's trade surplus fell a year-on-year 17.85 percent to $2.37 billion in the first two months of this year. \par \par \uc2  Exports rose 14.5 percent year-on-year in January and February while imports gained 17.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said more players were adopting a wait-and-see attitude amid expectations of further slowing of growth of foreign trade for the rest of this year. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, turnover was slim at only $150 million, although that was up from Tuesday's $90 million, according the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's website, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com.cn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com.cn}}}\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The figures compared with an average daily turnover of $402 million for February, according to exchange data. \par \par \uc2  Foreign Trade Minister Shi Guangsheng said on Tuesday trade growth was likely to slow in 2001 due to a weaker global economy. \par \par \uc2  "The growth rate of China's foreign trade in this year is likely to slow down due to slowing global economic growth and the high base of the rapid growth of China's foreign trade in the past two years," Shi said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was likely to move narrowly around present levels in thin trade in the near term. \par \par \uc2  They said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push up or depress the yuan on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the yuan in the wafer-thin trading band of 8.2770 and 8.2800 through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for about three years, partly to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But the bank has reduced its activity in the last year, allowing the yuan to close outside the usual range more than 40 times since April 2000, although only twice outside the weak end. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say Beijing is moving towards a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to cushion China from trade shocks after its entry to the World Trade Organisation, probably this year. \par \par \uc2  But they say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems more willing to test a wider trading range when the yuan breaches the strong end of the band and tends to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more readily when the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceeds the weak end. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan weakened to close at 6.9764 against 100 Japanese yen from 6.8839 on Tuesday. It ended unchanged at 1.0610 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3e044um\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
