\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc59}{\*\bkmkend toc59}\b \uc2  China yuan edges ahead, exporters unload dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 06:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, March 8 (Reuters) - China's yuan gained fresh ground against the U.S. dollar on Thursday in moderate trade as dollar sales by local exporters mounted. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2770 to one dollar, the strong end of its 30-notch trade band which the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has enforced through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for about three years. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at an intraday low of 8.2773, where it closed on Wednesday, and touched a high of 8.2769. Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2  Turnover grew to $230 million from a slow $130 million on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Since Monday, the yuan has reversed a week-long weakening as dollar supply shook off brief sluggishness that followed China's opening of its hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  B share markets to citizens with legal \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  savings on February 28. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said an anticipated surge in dollar demand had put psychological pressure on the yuan, although the official \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is still under rigid government control and the yuan is not convertible on the capital account. \par \par \uc2  While the impact from the stock market opening faded, growing dollar sales by domestic exporters also helped boost the yuan this week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Banks were selling more dollars today, but the bid side seemed slightly weaker," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Banks typically settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the national \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mostly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Since April 2000, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced its activity on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and allowed the yuan to close outside the usual range more than 40 times, although only twice outside the weak end of its normal range. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say Beijing is moving towards a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to cushion China from trade shocks after its entry to the World Trade Organisation, probably this year. \par \par \uc2  But the yuan was unlikely to fall through the key 8.2800 mark in the short term as Beijing appeared reluctant to stir any speculation of a yuan devaluation, they said. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the yuan strengthened against the yen to close at 6.8800 versus 6.9580. It also edged firmer against the Hong Kong dollar to end at 1.0609 versus 1.0612. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3804pac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
