\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc61}{\*\bkmkend toc61}\b \uc2  China's yuan ends down ahead of B share re-opening. \b0\par\par\uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2001\par 07:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Feb 26 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed weaker in thin trade on Monday as some banks conducted light dollar buying in anticipation of minor hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflows when domestic investors start trading B shares, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Domestic investors with legal \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank deposits will be allowed to trade hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  B shares, formerly reserved for foreigners, when the market reopens on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan closed at an intraday low of 8.2800 to the dollar, down from Friday's 8.2774. It touched a high of 8.2771. \par \par \uc2  There was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the yuan's weakness, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Turnover remained thin at $130 million, although that was up from Friday's slim $60 million, according to figures published by the market's website, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com.cn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com.cn}}}\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Some domestic banks bought dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as they expected their outstanding deposits to drop slightly due to the B share opening," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Trading in B shares has been suspended since the B share announcement a week ago to allow exchanges and brokerages to prepare for a new wave of traders. \par \par \uc2  Chinese investors have rushed to open B share trading accounts in anticipation of heavy gains after the Shanghai and Shenzhen B share markets re-open. \par \par \uc2  LIMITED \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  OUTFLOW SEEN \par \par \uc2  Although some $75 billion in individual \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits can now be channelled into the B share markets, dealers said actual \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflow would be limited. \par \par \uc2  The total market capitalisation of B share firms was $7.2 billion on February 19 when trading was suspended. The value of tradable shares was $6.3 billion. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect B shares to rise some 20 to 30 percent when markets reopen and this translated to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand of $1.3 billion to $1.9 billion, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "This amount is not large for many banks," said another local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Officials have also put restrictions in place to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflow. We've also seen new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits coming in for the B share opening," he said. \par \par \uc2  Beijing has banned Chinese investors from withdrawing hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from B share trading accounts or sending money out of the country. Shifting hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at home would also be limited to the same city and bank, state media said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move near the weak end of its normal wafer-thin trading range of 8.2770 to 8.2800 in the near term. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to contain the yuan in the slim trading band over the past three years, partly to quell speculation of a devaluation, though it has become less active since last year. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. Banks typically adjust their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with their corporate clients, mostly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan weakened slightly to end at 7.1400 to 100 Japanese yen from 7.0999 on Friday. It strengthened slightly against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0606 versus 1.0613. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx2q057h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
