\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc63}{\*\bkmkend toc63}\b \uc2  China Yuan Higher On Exporter Buying; Bonds Mostly Down \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2001\par 09:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan Friday finished stronger against the dollar on buying by exporters, with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling to CNY8.2768 compared with Thursday's 8.2774. \par \par \uc2  "Banks on behalf of exporters dominated the market again, showing they have surplus dollars," said a trader at Shanghai Pudong Development bank. \par \par \uc2  By Chinese law, most exporters must repatriate 85% of their overseas receipts to state-owned banks. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was stuck between CNY8.2766 and CNY8.2771, with US$60 million changing hands during the session, slightly lower than the US$80 million Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Importer buying lent some support to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its downside, although the volume of such trading was low. \par \par \uc2  "We saw some importers' dollar buyings dealt around CNY8.2770 during the session," said a trader at Industrial & Commercial Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't detected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  the market, traders said. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan is closely watched by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and can only be exchanged for business purposes. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar slid to CNY1.0612 from CNY1.0660. The Japanese yen dropped to CNY7.1556 per 100 yen from CNY7.1571. \par \par \uc2  Government bonds settled mostly lower on profit-taking, with the 1997 10-year bond, the biggest loser, slumping CNY0.42 to CNY137.86. \par \par \uc2  The 1997 issue, which had been rising sharply in the three previous sessions on institutional buying, fell CNY1.05 at one point in the morning to an intraday low of CNY137.23. \par \par \uc2  "As there's no news to increase investors' buying interest for the time being, profit-taking can be triggered by any slight gains" in previous sessions, said a trader at Shenyin & Wanguo Securities in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  The 1999 eight-year bond shed CNY0.04 to CNY100.40. The 2000 10-year floating-rate bond which jumped CNY0.13 to CNY102.61 on trade of 68,818 lots. \par \par \uc2  Volume in bond market totaled CNY810 million, less than the CNY1.11 billion posted Thursday. \par \par \uc2  China's bond market is off-limits to foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx2g00q3o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
