\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc64}{\*\bkmkend toc64}\b \uc2  China's yuan ends down as banks buy dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2001\par 07:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Feb 15 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened against the U.S. dollar on Thursday as local banks unwound positions in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been strong for weeks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2774 to the dollar, down from 8.2763 on Wednesday. It hit an intraday high of 8.2762 and a low of 8.2774. \par \par \uc2  There was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan had been strong over the past few days as local banks sold dollars on behalf of exporters and pushed it near 8.2761, the highest close since China set up the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and unifed its dual exchange systems in 1994. \par \par \uc2  "As the yuan climbed over the past few sessions, dollar demand had weakened in thin trade and worries over dollar weakness picked up," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Some local banks conducted light buying in dollars today to help boost sentiment in the dollar. But dollar demand still lags behind supply," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said despite the yuan's strength on Thursday, caution over possible weakness dollar continued to loom, leading to a wait-and-see attitude. \par \par \uc2  Turnover remained extremely thin at only $80 million against a slim $50 million on Wednesday, according the market's website, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com.cn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com.cn}}}\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  After the market closed on Wednesday, Beijing announced that China had a trade surplus of $1.375 billion in January, down from $1.5 billion a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said despite the fall, the surplus indicated a continued strong inflow of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the Shanghai-based national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. But the surplus had been expected and factored into yuan exchange rates, they said. \par \par \uc2  Trade is key to deciding dollar supply and demand on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Banks usually adjust their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the national market after trading the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mainly exporters and importers. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was likely to move narrowly around the 8.2770 level in the near term, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has enforced a wafer-thin trading range of 8.2770 to 8.2800 for the past three years, partly to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But the bank has relaxed its rigid control over the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, allowing the yuan to close outside its normal thin band 40 times since April 2000, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have quietly set a new strong end for the yuan's movements, possibly at 8.2760, as it tests the waters for a wider trading range. \par \par \uc2  Chinese officials say they are considering a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to cushion trade shocks related to entry to the World Trade Organisation, expected this year. They have given no timetable for a wider trading band. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll in December showed most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would allow the yuan to flow in a range of five percent up or down by end-2001, compared with a fraction of less than one percent at present. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the yuan weakened against the Japanese yen to close at 7.1571 versus 7.0718 on Wednesday. It also weakened to end at 1.0660 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0608. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx2f06li9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
