\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc66}{\*\bkmkend toc66}\b \uc2  China yuan ends firmer in sluggish dollar demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2001\par 06:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Feb 5 (Reuters) - China's yuan strengthened in sleepy trade against the U.S. dollar on Monday due to the absence of active dollar demand from domestic importers. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2771 to the dollar, compared with 8.2780 on Friday, and it moved in a mere four-notch intraday range of 8.2768 to 8.2772. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar sales showed signs of picking up on Monday, but sluggish demand from importers for the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped boost the yuan and kept trade thin. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar sales seemed to be getting stronger today, but the demand side still remained weak," said a dealer at an European Bank in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. Banks usually adjust their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the national market after trading the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mainly exporters and importers. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has generally regained its strength since the Shanghai-based market reopened last Wednesday after being closed from January 24-30 for the Chinese New Year holiday. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, turnover eased to a paltry $40 million from Friday's slim $50 million, according to the official market website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com.cn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com.cn}}}\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Many firms only got back to work on Monday after the holiday anbd dealers said they expected \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade to become more active later this week as banks and companies resumed normal business \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan within a razor-thin band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 for about three years after the Asian economic crisis, partly to quell speculation of a yuan devaluation. \par \par \uc2  As China moves close to its entry to the World Trade Organisation, which economists say will cause shocks to the country's trade performance, Beijing appeared to have been loosening its iron grip on the yuan. \par \par \uc2  Since April 2000, the yuan has closed outside the usual trading band more than 30 times and it hit a weak 8.2810 on January 23, outside the soft end of its trading band. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Officials have said the government is considering a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to cushion the impact from trade shocks related to China's WTO membership. But they have given no time table or official announcement on widening the yuan band. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll in December showed most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would allow the yuan to flow in a range of five percent up or down by the end of 2001, compared with a fraction of less than one percent at present. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was likely to remain strong in the near term as China's healthy trade surplus last year had produced abundant dollar supply. \par \par \uc2  Against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan firmed on Friday against the yen to close at 7.1420 versus 7.2076. It closed unchanged at 1.0606 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx25060dp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
