\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc67}{\*\bkmkend toc67}\b \uc2  China's yuan ends weaker in thin trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2001\par 05:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Feb 2 (Reuters) - China's yuan eased against the U.S. dollar on Friday, but dealers said the fall did not represent a trend due to thin trade after a long holiday. \par \par \uc2  They said the yuan would still be supported by a strong dollar supply on the national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and was likely to rise slightly next week. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at an intraday low of 8.2780 to the dollar on Friday, compared with 8.2774 on Thursday. It touched an intraday high of 8.2768. \par \par \uc2  Turnover was only $50 million, down from an already thin $120 million, according to the market website, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com.cn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com.cn}}}\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Dollar buying by a handful of local banks late in the session made the yuan close down slightly today," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  "But trade was thin and the fall did not represent a trend," he said. "Instead, there remains an oversupply of dollars on the market and the yuan is likely to rise next week." \par \par \uc2  The yuan has generally regained its strength after the Shanghai-based market reopened on Wednesday after being closed from January 24-30 for the long Chinese New Year holiday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some bank traders from other parts of China were still on holiday and trade was usually thin ahead of weekends. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has recovered after closing at a weak 8.2810 on January 23 in thin trade ahead of the holiday - outside the weak end of the yuan's normal thin trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  The central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan within that razor-thin band for about three years after the Asian economic crisis, partly to quell speculation of a devaluation of the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. The bank has relaxed its control over the yuan's movements since last year, allowing it to close outside the normal trading band more than 30 times since April 2000. \par \par \uc2  Officials have said the government is considering a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to cushion the impact from trade shocks related to China's entry into the World Trade Organisation, probably later this year. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll in December showed most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would allow the yuan to flow in a range of five percent up or down by the end of 2001, compared with a fraction of less than one percent at present. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was likely to rise slightly in the near term to move around the 8.2770 level because China's strong foreign trade surplus had produced ample dollar supply. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is convertible only on the current account. Banks usually settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions on the national market after trading yuan with corporate clients, mainly exporters and importers. \par \par \uc2  Against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan weakened to close Friday at 7.2076 against the Japanese yen from Thursday's 7.1100. \par \par \uc2  It closed little changed at 1.0606 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0605. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx2205wec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoa