\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc69}{\*\bkmkend toc69}\b \uc2  China yuan edges up in sluggish trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2001\par 05:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Jan 31 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday in thin trade on the first day of business after the Lunar New Year holiday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2786 to the U.S. doller after ending at 8.2810 on January 23, when it closed outside the weak end of its normal trading band for the first time since April 2000. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the U.S. dollar backed away from its January 23 close after major institutional traders returned to their desks after the holidays. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com}}}\uc2  reported sluggish turnover of $160 million, up a whisker from a low $100 million on January 23. \par \par \uc2  "There's not much activity in yuan today," said one foreign dealer. "There's no real direction ... The minor fluctuations we've seen are normal." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they saw no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dealers said the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been less active in the market in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  Following the Asian economic crisis, the bank kept the yuan within a razor-thin trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 for about three years through periodic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Beijing has pledged to give the yuan more leeway to cope with potential shocks after China joins the World Trade Organisation, expected in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is convertible only on the current account and banks usually settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions on the national market after trading yuan with corporate clients, mostly exporters and importers. \par \par \uc2  Against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan climbed further against the Japanese yen to close at 7.0325 against 7.0720 on January 23. \par \par \uc2  It ended virtually flat against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0606 versus 1.0604 on January 22, the last day of trade before the break. \par \par \uc2   SPEED GUIDES \par \par \uc2   RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  China news\tab \tab \tab    Shenzhen stock report\tab \par  Greater China news\tab \tab  Shanghai stock report\tab \par  Hong Kong news\tab \tab      Chinese hot stocks\tab \par  Taiwan news\tab \tab \tab   Chinese diary\tab \tab \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab      Chinese summary\tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press digests .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1v079iv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
