\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc74}{\*\bkmkend toc74}\b \uc2  China's yuan slips,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  support seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2001\par 05:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Jan 8 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened sharply against the U.S. dollar on Monday in slow trade and dealers said there were signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the yuan at the key 8.2800 mark. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2787 to one dollar just minutes after hitting its intraday low of 8.2800. It ended at 8.2771 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said scant dollar supply helped weigh down the yuan, but the retreat might not indicate a near-term weakening trend. Market sluggishness early in a new year usually keeps the yuan directionless. \par \par \uc2  "When the yuan hit the 8.2800 level only a few minutes before the market close, some dollar sales came in to lift it swiftly by nearly 20 notches," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "It looked like the way the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had long capped the yuan in a tight trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But since April, the yuan has closed outside the strong end of the long-standing band 25 times. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Beijing was testing the waters for a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to offset trade shocks expected from its membership to World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  China expects to join the global trade club in the next few months and has said it is considering a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime. But it has given no timetable. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll in December found most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts expected China to widen the trading range to as much as five percent up or down by end-2001, compared to the current fraction of one percent. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said they expected Beijing to hold the yuan at the psychological 8.2800 mark until the impact of China WTO entry becomes clear. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. Banks usually adjust \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mostly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said domestic firms had been sidelined since the New Year holidays and market turnover could remain light this week. On Monday, dollar/yuan turnover climbed to a still thin $92 million from Friday's $53 million. \par \par \uc2  The yuan softened against the yen to close at 7.1008 versus 7.1001 on Friday. But it ended firmer against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0603, compared with 1.0610. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1804dkl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
