\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc75}{\*\bkmkend toc75}\b \uc2  China's yuan ends weaker, unfazed by Fed rate cut. \b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2001\par 06:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Jan 4 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened sharply against the U.S. dollar in thin trade on Thursday to close at 8.2785, back within its normal trading band, under pressure from sporadic dollar demand from domestic importers. \par \par \uc2  Trade in the tightly controlled \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was not affected by the U.S. Federal Reserve's surprise interest rate cut on Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Fed cut its key funds rate for overnight bank loans by half a percentage point and said it was prepared to cut further if needed to prevent the U.S. economy from slowing too much. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the yuan closed at 8.2785 to the U.S. dollar, compared to 8.2769 on Wednesday after swinging in a volatile intraday range of 8.2742 and 8.2799. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan, largely insulated from moves in global \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets due to China's rigid \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, was hit by dollar demand from importers. \par \par \uc2  "The market was not active at the beginning of the year, so even a small number of dollar buying orders could pull down the yuan," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. Banks usually adjust \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mostly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no clear trend for the yuan this week due to post-holiday sluggishness. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yuan turnover contracted to $45 million from an already slow $120 million on Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan capped in a tiny trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 for nearly three years. Dealers said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Since April, the yuan has closed outside the strong end of the long-standing band 25 times. Analysts said Beijing was testing the waters for a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to offset trade shocks expected from accession to World Trade Organisation. \par \par \uc2  China expects to join the global trade group in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll in December found most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts expected China to widen the trading range to as much as five percent up or down by end-2001, compared to the current fraction of a percent. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the yuan lost ground against the yen to close at 7.2700 versus 7.2248 on Wednesday. It also weakened against the Hong Kong dollar to end at 1.0615 from 1.0605. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1405psr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
