\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc76}{\*\bkmkend toc76}\b \uc2  China's yuan rises out of usual range. \b0\par\par\uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2001\par 05:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Jan 3 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed firmer against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, out of its normal wafer-thin trading band due to an ample supply of dollars on the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at an intraday high of 8.2769 to the dollar, up from 8.2779 on Tuesday, and out of its normal tight trading band of 8.2770 and 8.2800 which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has enforced over the past three years. It touched an intraday low of 8.2781. \par \par \uc2  "There is an abundant dollar supply on the market due to China's strong exports and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves last year," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. Banks usually adjust \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions on the national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mostly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Official figures said China had a foreign trade surplus of $23.5 billion in the first 11 months of last year as exports surged 30.1 percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were $163.9 billion at the end of November 2000, up from $154.7 billion at the beginning of the year, the figures showed. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's market turnover remained thin at $120 million, although that was up from $110 million on Tuesday, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com}}}\uc2 , the website of the Shanghai-based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trade was usually thin at the start of a year because business needs were reduced as banks usually traded heavily in December for annual \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlement. \par \par \uc2  There was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan sandwiched in a thin trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 until it allowed the yuan to weaken outside the range in April 2000. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has since closed outside the strong end of the long-standing band 25 times, including this time on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say Beijing has been testing the waters for a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to offset shocks on its trade performance after joining the World Trade Organisation, which China expects in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  China has said it is considering a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime though has not given a timetable. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll last week found most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts expected China to widen the trading range to as much as five percent up or down by end-2001, compared to the current fraction of a percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was likely to close out the strong end of its long-standing thin trading band again in the near term due to strong dollar supply on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the yuan's upward trend if it tended to close stronger than its historical high of 8.2764 set on May 24, 2000, they said. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan firmed slightly against the yen to close at 7.2248, compared with 7.2298 on Tuesday. It also ended a touch firmer versus the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0605 from 1.0608. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1306u9l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
