\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc77}{\*\bkmkend toc77}\b \uc2  China's yuan firms slightly in thin trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 2001\par 06:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Jan 2 (Reuters) - China's yuan edged firmer against the U.S. dollar on Monday as thin trade typical of the start of the year sidelined most bank traders, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2779 to the dollar, compared with 8.2780 on Friday. It moved narrowly for the entire session, touching an intraday high of 8.2771 and a low of 8.2783. \par \par \uc2  Turnover remained thin at $110 million, although that was up from $58 million on Friday according to figures issued by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com}}}\uc2 , the website of the Shanghai-based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The market was closed on Monday for the New Year holiday. \par \par \uc2  "Trade on the market is typically slow around the start of a new year as banks have just completed settling all their 2000 trades in December," said a U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Amid thin trade, both buyers and sellers have no intention of pushing the yuan up or down sharply today," he said. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. Banks usually adjust \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions on the national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mostly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept the yuan sandwiched in a wafer-thin trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 for three years until it allowed the yuan to weaken outside the range in April 2000. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has since closed outside the strong end of the long-standing band 24 times. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say Beijing has been testing the waters for a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to offset shocks on its trade performance after joining the World Trade Organisation, which China expects in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, two \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  researchers urged the government to allow the yuan to fluctuate in a range of 10 to 15 percent up or down as it moves towards a more flexible exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  It was the first time anyone connected to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had offered a specific range for widening the trading band. The range was much wider than what private analysts were forecasting. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll last week found most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts expected China to widen the trading range to as much as five percent up or down by end-2001, compared to the current fraction of a percent. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman told Reuters on Friday there had been no change in China's exchange rate policy and the opinions aired by the researchers did not reflect official positions. \par \par \uc2  China has said it was considering a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime though has not given a timetable. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yuan weakened slightly against the yen to close at 7.2298, compared with 7.2100 on Friday. It also ended a touch weaker versus the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0608 from 1.0604. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1207gnd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
