\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc78}{\*\bkmkend toc78}\b \uc2  China yuan little changed in thin year-end trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2000\par 06:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Dec 28 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed little changed against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, with demand for year-end settlement transactions drying up as the year winds down, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2786 to one dollar versus 8.2785 on Wednesday after moving in a range of 8.2772 to 8.2792. \par \par \uc2  Turnover remained thin at $162 million on Thursday, though that was up from a slim $105 million on Wednesday, according to figures issued by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com}}}\uc2 , the website of the Shanghai-based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  There was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Domestic banks are required to finish their annual \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlement by Friday," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "The overwhelming majority of them had done so by early this week. Trading on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market today was dominated by sporadic needs," he said. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account. Banks usually adjust \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions on the national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mostly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has risen over the past few weeks, moving around the strong end of its normal thin trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 due to increased dollar selling from trade companies. \par \par \uc2  Dollar sales typically rise in the last few weeks of a year as Chinese trade firms conduct year-end settlement, and exports peak during the Christmas and New Year holidays. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sandwiched in the 30-notch bank for nearly three years, partly to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But since May 23, the bank has eased its iron grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , allowing it to close just outside the firm end of its usual band 24 times, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts this week found most expect China will widen the trading range for the yuan to as much as five percent up or down by end-2001, compared with its current de facto band of a fraction of one percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say Beijing has been testing the waters for a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to offset the potential impact on its trade performance coming from membership in the World Trade Organisation, which China expects in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the yuan strengthened against the yen to close at 7.2177, compared with 7.2543 on Wednesday. It ended almost unchanged at 1.0607 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0606. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwcs08vnt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
