\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc80}{\*\bkmkend toc80}\b \uc2  China yuan weakens as exporters grip dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2000\par 05:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Dec 27 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed weaker against the U.S. dollar in thin trade on Wednesday as dollar selling by exporters eased, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at an intraday low of 8.2785 to one dollar versus 8.2768 on Tuesday, back in its thin 30-notch band that the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  enforced through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for nearly three years. \par \par \uc2  There was no sign of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan moved in a narrow range for the entire session, touching an intraday high of 8.2768. \par \par \uc2  Turnover plunged to $105 million from $207 million, according to figures issued by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com}}}\uc2 , the website of the Shanghai-based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar selling by exporters eased today as reflected by thinner turnover," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  "Trade firms seemed to have settled most of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions over the past few weeks. The yuan is likely to move narrowly around the current levels in thin trade before the end of the year," he said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan has risen over the past few weeks, moving around the strong end of its normal thin trading band of 8.2770 to 8.2800 due to increased dollar selling from trade companies. \par \par \uc2  Dollar sales typically rise in the last few weeks of a year as Chinese trade firms conduct year-end settlement, and exports peak during the Christmas and New Year holidays. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account and banks usually adjust \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against it on the national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mostly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sandwiched between 8.2770 and 8.2800 for nearly three years, partly to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But since May 23, the bank had eased its iron grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , allowing it to close just outside the firm end of its usual band 24 times, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers speculated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  already had quietly widened the firm end of the band by two notches to 8.2768. \par \par \uc2  There has been no official comment on such a change. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say Beijing is testing the waters for a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to offset the potential impact on its trade performance coming from membership in the World Trade Organisation, which China expects in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  The WTO accession is expected to lead to a rise in China's imports and consequently exert pressure on the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan strengthened against the yen to close at 7.2543, compared with 7.2811 on Tuesday. It ended almost unchanged at 1.0606 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0605. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwcr095q2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
