\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc81}{\*\bkmkend toc81}\b \uc2  China yuan inches firmer, ends outside its band. \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 2000\par 06:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Dec 26 (Reuters) - China's yuan gained fresh ground against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday, closing outside the strong end of its long-standing trade band for the 24th time in the past seven months. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2768 to one dollar versus Monday's 8.2770 - the firm end of the 30-notch band that the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  enforced through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for nearly three years. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was underpinned by flush dollar supply as domestic exporters kept unloading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings for book-closing. There were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Tuesday, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan continued to be stable at around 8.2770 today because dollar sales have been consistently rich so far this month," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan is convertible only on the current account and banks usually adjust \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against it on the national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mostly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  China kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sandwiched between 8.2770 and 8.2800 for nearly three years. But since May 23, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has eased its iron grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , allowing it to close just outside the firm end of its usual band 24 times. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers speculate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  already had stealthily widened the firm end of the band by two notches to 8.2768. There has been no official comment on such a change. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say Beijing is testing the waters for a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to offset the potential impact on its trade performance expected from membership in the World Trade Organisation. China expects to join the WTO in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yuan strengthened against the yen to close at 7.2811, compared with 7.3500 on Monday. It ended unchanged at 1.0605 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwcq094p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
