\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc83}{\*\bkmkend toc83}\b \uc2  China Yuan Ends Flat; Bonds Mostly Dn On IPOs \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2000\par 09:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan ended unchanged Friday at CNY8.2768 to the U.S. dollar, with the yuan consistently trading above the strong end of its implicit trading band, due to the seasonal rise in exports, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Government bonds settled mostly lower on expectations that a spate of initial public offerings and share issues by companies would continue until yearend, diverting money from fixed income instruments. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened at its intraday low of CNY8.2701, the product of a stray deal by one bank eager to get local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. It was the lowest intraday level for the dollar since Nov. 8 when it fell to CNY8.2675. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's intraday high was CNY8.2769. Turnover in the yuan/dollar market was US$240 million, down from US$280 million Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still pressured by ample dollar supply, reflecting the fact exporters are actively selling their products overseas," said a trader at Industrial & Commercial Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  She said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally keeps a close eye on yuan/dollar trading and tries to keep the exchange rate within a 8.2770-8.2800 band. \par \par \uc2  In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Hong Kong dollar inched higher to CNY1.0610 from CNY1.0608. The yen added to CNY7.3675 per 100 yen from CNY7.3513. \par \par \uc2  Trading volume in the government bond market shrank to CNY2.4 billion, as compared with Thursday's CNY3.09 billion. \par \par \uc2  Only the 2000 seven-year floating-rate bond was up, gaining CNY0.03 to CNY100.04 on trade of 371,315 lots. The other seven listed bonds closed lower as investors looked to IPOs and new share issues in coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  "Usually, the government allows more companies to offer shares to the public in late December, otherwise firms have to re-audit their financial data next year... Bond investors are preparing to subscribe to those IPOs," said a trader at Shenyin & Wanguo Securities in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  The 2000 ten-year floating-rate bond retreated CNY0.05 to CNY102.85 on trade of 202,548 lots. \par \par \uc2  The 1999 ten-year bond edged CNY0.01 down to CNY100.67 on trade of 1,044,914 lots. Its yield was flat at 3.31%. \par \par \uc2  China's bond market is off-limits to foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwcf061cs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
