\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc85}{\*\bkmkend toc85}\b \uc2  China Yuan Weakens As Importers Reemerge; Bonds Mostly Dn \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2000\par 09:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan closed weaker at CNY8.2792 to the U.S. dollar Monday as against CNY8.2768 Friday, as importers resurfaced to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late session after several days of absence, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Government bonds closed mostly lower, with several bonds succumbing to profit-taking. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar vacillated between CNY8.2769 and CNY8.2792 during the session, although a trader at Shanghai Pudong Development Bank said most transactions were dealt around CNY8.2770. \par \par \uc2  "Active dollar-buying gradually nudged the dollar to close higher," a trader at Industrial & Commercial Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  said, adding the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  Turnover in the yuan/dollar market reached US$120 million, sharply higher than US$30 million Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said they haven't read or heard of a state media report about a slight slowdown in export growth during the first 11 months of the year. Exports in the first 11 months this year grew 30.1%, slower than 32.2% growth in the first 10 months. \par \par \uc2  Major securities newspapers didn't carry the report in their Monday edition. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan can only be converted for current account transactions. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar inched higher to CNY1.0610 from CNY1.0607. The yen fell to CNY7.4540 per Y100 from CNY7.4701. \par \par \uc2  In the bond market, five bond issues closed lower on profit-taking, while only two issues ended higher. \par \par \uc2  "Investors are focusing on IPOs again," a trader at Shanghai Finance Securities said. \par \par \uc2  Two companies, which plan to raise CNY607.6 million, launched their initial public offerings Monday. \par \par \uc2  Bonds are expected to slide further in the coming sessions as China's largest steel company, Baoshan Iron & Steel Co., will list Tuesday and three new IPOs will start their offerings Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The 2000 10-year floating-rate bond shed CNY0.07 to CNY102.70 on trade of 152,528 lots. \par \par \uc2  The 1999 10-year bond fell CNY0.45 to CNY100.25 on trade of 238,342 lots. Its yield advanced to 3.36% from 3.30%. \par \par \uc2  The 2000 seven-year floating-rate bond gained CNY0.03 to CNY100.01 on trade of 461,739 lots. \par \par \uc2  Trading volume reached CNY1.76 billion, slightly higher than Friday's CNY1.50 billion. \par \par \uc2  China's bond market is off-limits to foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21)6218-3268; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwcb05xzo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
