\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc86}{\*\bkmkend toc86}\b \uc2  China's yuan ends outside band, c.bank takes break. \b0\par\par\uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2000\par 05:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Dec 8 (Reuters) - China's yuan strengthened to close outside its normal wafer-thin band of 8.2770 to 8.2880 as trade firms continued to dump the dollar for settlement, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  as volume eased, they said. The bank had stepped in to check the yuan each day from Monday to Thursday, driving it back to close inside its band. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the yuan closed at 8.2768 to the dollar, compared with 8.2772 on Thursday. It moved in a narrow range of 8.2700 and a high of 8.2767, trading outside the strong end of its long-standing band for most of the session. \par \par \uc2  Turnover fell sharply to $30 million from an already thin $50 million on Thursday, partly because bank traders had settled most of their positions early this week, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar selling from trade firms continued to dominate the market today," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept on the sidelines, partly because thin trade already made the yuan move in a narrow range," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar selling typically rises at the end of the year because trade firms conduct annual settlement and exports rise to meet Christmas and New Year demand, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  For the past week, the yuan has been moving around the strong end of its razor-thin range, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has enforced through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for three years. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was likely to remain strong and move around 8.2770 next week, dealers said. But they said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step in to slap the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into line if it appeared ready to breach its historical high close of 8.2764. \par \par \uc2  Despite the bank's increased activity over the past few days, dealers said it appeared to have cut down on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. The yuan has ended outside the strong end of its normal band about 20 times since May. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the bank was moving towards a wider band as China drew close to membership in the World Trade Organisation, expected in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  WTO accession would lead to rising imports and exert downward pressure on the yuan, they said. \par \par \uc2  Beijing has vowed to pursue a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to prepare for WTO entry, but has given no timetable. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the yuan strengthened a touch against the yen to 7.4701 per 100 yen from Thursday's 7.4827. It closed unchanged at 1.0607 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwc80anpu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
