\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc87}{\*\bkmkend toc87}\b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan ends down on c. bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2000\par 06:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Dec 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan weakened against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into check the yuan's strength, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at an intraday low of 8.2773 to the dollar, compared with 8.2770 on Tuesday. It touched a high of 8.2767 and traded outside the strong end of its long-standing band for most of the session. \par \par \uc2  "There was clear evidence that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying dollars whenever the yuan rose above 8.2770," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "The bank seems to have strengthened its activity over the past few sessions as increasing dollar selling at the year-end is pushing the yuan up steadily," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar selling typically rises at the end of a year because trade firms conduct annual settlement and exporters increase business to meet Christmas and New Year demand, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rise has pushed up the yuan over the past week to move around the strong end of its razor-thin range between 8.2770 and 8.2800, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has enforced through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past three years. \par \par \uc2  Turnover on Wednesday rose to $240 million from $200 million on Tuesday, according to figures published by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com}}}\uc2 , the website of the China Foreign Trade Trade System market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to remain strong and move around 8.2770 in the near term. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to prevent it from topping its historical high close of 8.2764 set on May 24, they said. \par \par \uc2  Despite its increased activity over the past few days, dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have reduced its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year as a whole. The yuan has ended outside the strong end of its normal band about 20 times since May. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the bank was moving towards a wider band as China drew close to membership in the World Trade Organisation, expected in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  WTO accession would lead to rising imports and exert downward pressure on the yuan, they said. \par \par \uc2  Beijing has vowed to pursue a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to prepare for WTO entry, but has given no timetable. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan weakened against the yen to 7.5000 per 100 yen from Tuesday's 7.4480. It closed slightly firmer at 1.0606 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0609. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwc60b3qj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
