\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc88}{\*\bkmkend toc88}\b \uc2  China's yuan inches up, trade firms sell dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2000\par 05:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Dec 5 (Reuters) - China's yuan closed a notch firmer against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday, ending right at the strong end of its wafer-thin trading band as domestic trade firms sold the greenback, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said there were signs that the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the session to check the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upward trend but others were not aware of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2770 to the dollar, compared with 8.2771 on Monday after moving in a narrow range of 8.2767 and 8.2771. \par \par \uc2  "Trade firms have been selling dollars over the past sessions partly due to increased export earnings and year-end settlement," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Chinese trade firms are required to settle most of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings through local banks designated to trade on the market. The value of the yuan is mainly driven by China's trade performance as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Turnover on Tuesday plunged to $200 million from a heavy $410 million on Monday, according to figures published by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com}}}\uc2 , the website of the China Foreign Trade Trade System market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Mondays were typically active after the weekend trading halt. \par \par \uc2  A second local bank dealer said there were persistent yuan selling bids on Tuesday, a sign of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The yuan stayed above the 8.2770 level for most of the session today, a possible reason for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  For nearly three years, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has enforced a razor-thin band of 8.2770 and 8.2800 partly to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have reduced its activity over the past few months. The yuan has ended outside the strong end of its normal band about 20 times since May. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the bank was moving towards a wider band as China drew close to membership in the World Trade Organisation, expected in next few months. WTO accession would lead to rising imports and exert downward pressure on the yuan. \par \par \uc2  Beijing has vowed to pursue a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to prepare for WTO entry, but has given no timetable. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to remain strong because dollar selling typically rises due to settlement at the end of a year and exports increase to meet Christmas and New Year demand. \par \par \uc2  They expected the yuan to close outside the 8.2770 level this week, breaching the strong end of its usual tight trading band. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to prevent it from topping its historical high close of 8.2764 set on May 24, they said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yuan closed little changed against the yen at 7.4480 from Monday's 7.4454. It also ended almost unchanged at 1.0609 against the Hong Kong dollar from 1.0610. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwc50begm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\