\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc89}{\*\bkmkend toc89}\b \uc2  China's yuan inches up,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  pushes back. \b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2000\par 06:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Dec 4 (Reuters) - China's yuan gained ground against the U.S. dollar on Monday, ending near the strong end of its wafer-thin trading band as domestic exporters sold dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in heavy trade late in the session to check the yuan's upward trend, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2771 to the dollar, compared with 8.2772 on Friday. It hit an intraday high of 8.2755 and a low of 8.2774. \par \par \uc2  Turnover surged to $410 million from a $1.99 million, a sign of strong foreign trade volume, which according to official figures is up more than 30 percent in the first 10 months of 2000. \par \par \uc2  For nearly three years, the yuan has been boxed within a razor-thin band of 8.2770 and 8.2800, a range enforced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  partly to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen in the market today as the yuan showed signs of continued strength due to exporter dollar selling," said a local bank dealer. "Active transactions are a sign of continued robust foreign trade." \par \par \uc2  The value of the yuan is mainly driven by China's trade performance as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to remain strong in the near term, noting that exporters typically ship more goods overseas to meet Christmas and New Year demand and wind up with more dollars to sell. \par \par \uc2  Some expected the yuan to breach the 8.2770 level this week, the strong end of its usual tight trading band. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to prevent it from topping its historical high close of 8.2764 set on May 24. \par \par \uc2  Despite Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have reduced its activity. The yuan has closed outside the strong end of its normal band about 20 times since May. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the bank was moving towards a wider band as China drew close to membership in the World Trade Organisation, which would affect China's trade performance. \par \par \uc2  Officials have pledged to pursue a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to prepare for WTO membership, but have given no timetable. China hopes to join the global trade group in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan rose against the yen to close at 7.4454 from Friday's 7.5047. It ended unchanged at 1.0610 against the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwc40bgva\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
