\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc91}{\*\bkmkend toc91}\b \uc2  China's yuan ends weaker as importers seek dollars. \b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2000\par 05:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Nov 30 (Reuters) - China's yuan fell against the U.S. dollar on Thursday as importer demand for the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grew. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at its intraday low of 8.2797 to the dollar, compared with a 8.2775 close on Wednesday, after touching a session high of 8.2773 in early trade. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar buying orders flowed into the market steadily in late trade, pushing down the yuan through to the market close," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The value of the yuan is driven mainly by China's trade performance as it is convertible only on the current account. \par \par \uc2  Banks settle \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions against the yuan on the national market after trading hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with corporate clients, mostly importers and exporters. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the yuan is usually strong towards the end of the year as Chinese exporters ship more goods overseas to meet Christmas and New Year demand and have more dollars to sell. \par \par \uc2  But China's faster-than-expected economic growth this year might also drive up imports in the fourth quarter, which could offset the yuan's strength, they say. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the yuan eased out of its month-long firmness and bank traders reported fresh dollar demand from trade firms, a sign that imports were picking up. \par \par \uc2  For nearly three years, the yuan has been kept within a hair-thin band of 8.2770 and 8.2800 by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Since mid-April, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to have reduced its activity, allowing the yuan to end outside its normal band nearly 20 times. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say it is testing the waters for a wider band as China draws close to membership in the World Trade Organisation, which would affect China's trade performance. \par \par \uc2  Officials have pledged to pursue gradually a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime to prepare for China's WTO membership, but have given no timetable. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the yuan rose against the yen to close at 7.4410 from Wednesday's 7.5168. It also firmed against the Hong Kong dollar to end at 1.0609, compared with 1.0612 in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbu007zv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
