\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc95}{\*\bkmkend toc95}\b \uc2  China Yuan Stronger As Dlr Buying Eases; Bonds Mixed \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2000\par 09:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI -(Dow Jones)- China's yuan settled stronger at CNY8.2780 to the U.S. dollar Wednesday, from CNY8.2785 late Tuesday, as dollar buying by importers slowed, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Government bonds ended mixed as investors selectively sold bonds and put funds back in the stock markets. \par \par \uc2  The dollar traded between CNY8.2780 and CNY8.2786 during the half-day session. Turnover reached US$123 million, down from US$170 million Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A day after \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the dollar's sharp rise, "importer buying of dollars spontaneously eased," said a dealer at Shanghai Pudong Development Bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally keeps a close watch on yuan/dollar trading and tries to keep its trading within a thin 8.2770-8.2800 band. \par \par \uc2  In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Hong Kong dollar dipped to CNY1.0606 from CNY1.0608. The yen slipped to CNY7.3775 per 100 yen from CNY7.6260 in line with the yen's fall in international \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Rising share prices lured investors away from the bond market, said a trader at Shenyin & Wanguo Securities in Shanghai. \par \par \uc2  The biggest decliner was the 2000 ten-year floating-rate bond, which slipped CNY0.23 to CNY103.51 on trade of 18,381 lots. "The bond has gained for four straight days, causing more and more investors to lock in profits," the Shenyin trader said. \par \par \uc2  The 1997 ten-year bond inched a notch higher to CNY135.45 on trade of 125,892 lots. Its yield was flat at 4.05%. \par \par \uc2  Total volume in the market shrank to CNY1.53 billion, as compared with CNY1.95 billion Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  China's bond market is off-limits to foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  -By China Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; (86-21) 6218-3268; djnews.shanghai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwbm05ksd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
