\par\par {\*\bkmkstart toc97}{\*\bkmkend toc97}\b \uc2  China yuan weakens at close, back to thin band. \b0\par\par\uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2000\par 06:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Nov 10 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened slightly against the U.S. dollar on Friday, moving back into its usual wafer-thin trading band as dollar selling by exporters eased, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Thin trade ahead of the weekend led exporters to reduce their hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling, which had helped the yuan end outside the slim band of 8.2770 and 8.2800 three times in a week, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2772 to the dollar on Friday, down from 8.2768 on Thursday after moving in a range of 8.2769 and 8.2776. \par \par \uc2  Turnover fell to $1.9 million from $2.1 million, according to figures published by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.chinamoney.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.chinamoney.com}}}\uc2 , the market website of the China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System. \par \par \uc2  There were no signs of activity by the central People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past three years to keep the yuan in the tight range, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Thin trade ahead on Friday made the yuan's movements lack a clear direction," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "Easing dollar selling from exporters pushed the yuan to close weaker and within its normal trading band," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dollar settlement by exporters has pushed the yuan higher over the past few weeks. Chinese firms usually export more goods to Western countries in October and November to meet strong demand during the Christmas and New Year seasons. \par \par \uc2  Local trading firms are required to sell most of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings to state banks, which settle them on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  After the market closed on Friday, the official Xinhua news agency said China had a foreign trade surplus of $3.9 billion in October, down from $4.4 billion in the same month last year. \par \par \uc2  The surplus was $23.1 billion in January-October period, slightly lower than $23.8 billion a year earlier, Xinhua said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the surplus remained healthy despite the falls. \par \par \uc2  "Looking into these figures you can sense a strong inflow of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the market," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. "This explains the yuan's strength over the past few weeks." \par \par \uc2  Trade is key to decide dollar supply and demand on the market, as the yuan is only convertible on the current account. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed outside the strong end of its normal slim band on Thursday, Wednesday and last Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past few months had allowed the yuan to close outside the band more than a dozen times since mid-April. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be taking advantage of the yuan's strength to test a wider trading range. It takes a harder line when the yuan is soft, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop it from ending weaker than 8.2800 to quell speculation of a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Officials say China intends to make its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime more flexible to cushion shocks arising from the country's accession to the World Trade Organisation, which is expected in the next few months. There is no timetable. \par \par \uc2  In a Reuters poll of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts in July, six of 10 respondents said China would allow the yuan to trade in a broader range of at least plus or minus five percent by the end of 2001. Its current range is less than a fraction of one percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to remain strong next week, moving mainly between 8.2765 and 8.2770. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the yuan strengthened against the yen to close at 7.6725 to 100 yen versus Thursday's 7.8010. It ended marginally weaker against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0606 from 1.0604. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwba02771\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
